{"profile":{"name":"Gary Crawford","ward":"Ward 20, Scarborough Southwest","bio":"Gary Crawford was first elected to Toronto City Council in 2010, succeeding Brian Ashton in Scarborough Southwest, and re-elected in 2014, 2018 and 2022. Previously he served as a Toronto District School Board trustee (2003-2010) and worked as a professional artist and part-time musician before entering politics. As Mayor John Tory's budget chief from 2014 to 2023, he chaired the city's Budget Committee for nine years. He resigned from council in July 2023 to run as the Ontario Progressive Conservative candidate in the Scarborough-Guildwood provincial by-election and was defeated by Liberal candidate Andrea Hazell; his council seat was filled by Parthi Kandavel in the November 2023 by-election.","committees":["Budget Committee (Chair)","Executive Committee"],"contact":{"email":"councillor_crawford@toronto.ca","phone":"416-392-4052"},"promises":[{"text":"Ran on a platform centred on affordability, including keeping city spending under control as the city's long-serving budget chief.","source":"https://www.newspapers.com/article/the-toronto-star-municipal-election/186361067/"},{"text":"Ran on a platform centred on community safety as a core priority for Scarborough Southwest.","source":"https://www.newspapers.com/article/the-toronto-star-municipal-election/186361067/"},{"text":"Ran on a platform centred on 'maintaining the integrity of single-family homes,' pledging to protect the character of established residential neighbourhoods in Scarborough Southwest.","source":"https://www.newspapers.com/article/the-toronto-star-municipal-election/186361067/"}]},"lobbying":{"total":989,"term":64,"first":"2011-02-14","last":"2023-07-18","lobbyists":239,"clients":179,"subjects":445,"methods":{"Meetings":351,"Emails":461,"Phone calls":56,"Written":88,"Other or unreported":33},"top":[{"label":"Economic Development","count":286},{"label":"Licences / Licensing","count":153},{"label":"By-law / Regulation